; The mutation instrumenter, exposed as the dune instrumentation backend
; selected by --instrument-with ppx_windtrap.mutate.
;
; ONE library, naming ITSELF in (instrumentation.backend). Dune resolves
; --instrument-with <name> by looking up the library called <name> and
; reading its (instrumentation.backend) field; it does not object to that
; field naming the library that carries it. The RFC flagged this as an
; open question, so it was settled empirically before the shape was
; committed to: test/mutate_ppx/integration/ carries a library with the
; plain (instrumentation (backend ppx_windtrap.mutate)) stanza, and
;
;   dune exec --instrument-with ppx_windtrap.mutate \
;     test/mutate_ppx/integration/test_registration.exe
;
; grows the catalogue by that library's mutants - which it cannot do
; unless the backend resolved. The fallback the RFC named - a shell
; library carrying the field plus a separate rewriter library, the split
; ppx/dune + ppx/coverage/dune use - is therefore not needed here.
; Coverage is split for a different reason: its backend hangs off
; ppx_windtrap, whose OTHER job is the inline-test rewriter, and a
; library cannot be both a rewriter and a backend declaration for a
; DIFFERENT rewriter.
;
; ppx_runtime_libraries makes every instrumented library link the
; stdlib-only windtrap.runtime the generated code calls - and nothing
; else: instrumented user code must never pull the windtrap core into its
; closure.
;
; The library is also usable directly with (preprocess (pps
; ppx_windtrap.mutate)), which is what the golden expansion tests and the
; integration check under test/mutate_ppx use.

(library
 (name windtrap_mutate_ppx)
 (public_name ppx_windtrap.mutate)
 (kind ppx_rewriter)
 (libraries ppxlib)
 (ppx_runtime_libraries windtrap.runtime)
 (instrumentation.backend
  (ppx ppx_windtrap.mutate))
 (preprocess
  (pps ppxlib.metaquot)))
